Basics (selection & inspection)

Display the first 5 rows, the shape of the DataFrame, and the data types of each column.
Select only the employee and salary columns.
Show all employees who work in the IT department.
Show all employees older than 30 and earning more than 70,000.
Sort the DataFrame by salary in descending order.

Cleaning & transformation

Count how many missing values are in each column.
Fill the missing salaries with the average salary of the whole company.
Create a new column salary_pkr_lakh = salary divided by 100,000.
Create a column seniority that says "Senior" if years_at_company ≥ 10, otherwise "Junior" (hint: np.where or .apply).
